# OPD Patient Flow

## Purpose
OPD owns the outpatient encounter from arrival through consultation, tests, pharmacy, admission, referral, or discharge. Keep one active OPD encounter per patient and preserve source context on every handoff.

## Stage Sequence
- `WAITING_VITALS`: nurse triage and registration support.
- `WAITING_CONSULTATION_PAYMENT` or `WAITING_DOCTOR_ASSIGNMENT`: complete payment gate or assign provider.
- `WAITING_DOCTOR_REVIEW`: doctor consultation and clinical decision.
- `LAB_REQUESTED`, `RADIOLOGY_REQUESTED`, `PHARMACY_REQUESTED`: route to the sibling executing department flow.
- `WAITING_DISPOSITION`: doctor finalizes admit, refer, or discharge.
- `ADMITTED`: close OPD and hand off to IPD without duplicating the encounter.
- `DISCHARGED`: outpatient visit closed only.

## Handoffs
- Reception owns registration, check-in, and queue creation.
- Billing owns consultation and payment gates only.
- Nurse owns vitals and nurse-supported routing.
- Doctor owns clinical review and final disposition.
- OPD must hand off to `ipd-flow.mdc` when admitting; use `emergency-flow.mdc` only for preserved emergency context.

## Hard Invariants
- Must not create a second active OPD encounter for the same patient.
- Must not show department actions when the backend stage or role does not allow them.
- Must not expose raw enum names to users.
- Must keep OPD as the outpatient source record; inpatient, ICU, theater, nursing, discharge, lab, radiology, and pharmacy own their own work.

## Allowed Critical Actions
- Reuse shared workspace components before creating OPD-specific UI.
- Refresh only the affected row, detail panel, counts, and badges after small actions.
- Hide zero-count shortcuts when the workspace pattern expects that behavior.

